    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Atonement Crucible.</strong> You can build a forge hot enough to burn the worst parts off a story.</p><ul><li>Once per <strong>campaign arc</strong> (or other large narrative unit, at the GM’s discretion), you may lead a special <strong>atonement crafting</strong> project focused on a single <strong>Corrupted Spark</strong>.</li><li>Through days or weeks of work, ritual, and hard choices, you can attempt to <strong>purify</strong> that Corrupted Spark, transforming it into a <strong>redeemed</strong> or <strong>stabilized</strong> form instead of destroying it outright.</li><li>The exact mechanical consequences (Spark tags, Tikkun phases, Darkness shifts, faction reactions) are governed by your Spark/Tikkun engine, but this feature is the narrative permission slip: your forge can <em>save</em> a Spark instead of just breaking it.</li></ul>",
